'''Sant Chuan''', officially '''Sant Chuan d'os Baxos''' ({{Literal translation|{{W|John of Egypt|Saint John}} of the Lowlands}}) is a [[Cantons of Balisca|canton]]/city in the [[Xaraba]] region of [[Bayara]]. It is a major port on the [[Salsipuedes Sea]] and is considered an {{W|satellite city|accessory city}} to the larger [[Macaio|Macaio Metropolis]]. It recorded a population of 935,787 in the [[2025 Baliscan census|2025 census]], ranking as the third most-populous city in Bayara and the [[Largest cities in Balisca|14th-largest]] city in Balisca. 

